cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  RadiativeSurrogates.jl: reduced-basis neural surrogates for the heat
  equation with a nonlinear radiation boundary condition
type: software
authors:
  # TODO(Tom): before JOSS submission, replace with cited name and add ORCID
  - name: "Tommy (TommyDanMa)"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/TommyDanMa/RadiativeSurrogates.jl"
keywords:
  - reduced-order modeling
  - proper orthogonal decomposition
  - scientific machine learning
  - finite element method
  - thermal radiation
  - Julia
abstract: >-
  Reduced-basis neural surrogates for the heat equation with a nonlinear
  Stefan-Boltzmann radiation boundary condition (deep-space sink). Gridap
  assembles the finite element residuals and Jacobians; the SciML stack
  solves them (NonlinearSolve steady, OrdinaryDiffEq mass-matrix transient).
  The package carries a diagnostic methodology for deciding when coefficient
  learning is the right surrogate factorization: manifold spectrum
  measurement, pre-registered structural rank experiments, exact Galerkin
  error floors separating basis error from map error, and verification
  artifacts (grid-convergence error bands, seed ensembles, an
  out-of-distribution guard, a floating-point precision audit, and forward
  uncertainty propagation against an exact full-order Monte Carlo reference).
